title: The Falling Blocks template
intro: Pieces fall, rows clear, and it speeds up every ten rows, until they stack to the top. No code.
project: FallingBlocks | Stack Up

chapter: The game | A board, a HUD and a Game Over panel
scene: Game
say: The Falling Blocks template is a menu and this game scene, built from no-code pieces.
select: Board
explain: component:FallingBoard | Falling Board | A Falling Board, each shape landing as its own block tile.
explain: field:FallingBoard.Preview | Preview | It shows the next three pieces beside it.
select: Level
explain: component:Counter | Level | Counters show the score, the rows, and the level, which listens for Level Up.
select: Best
explain: field:Counter.SaveBestAs | Save Best As | The best score is saved, and the menu shows it too.
select: Game Over
explain: field:Panel.OpenMessage | Open Message | And this panel opens when the board sends Game Over.
expectvalue: Game Over.Panel.OpenMessage = Game Over
deselect

chapter: Play | Slide, turn and drop
play
wait: 1
tap: Left
wait: 0.2
tap: Left
wait: 0.2
tap: Space
wait: 0.5
tap: Up
wait: 0.2
tap: Right
wait: 0.2
tap: Right
wait: 0.2
tap: Space
wait: 0.5
tap: Space
wait: 0.8
expectvalue: Board.FallingBoard.GameOver = false
explain: game | Falling Blocks | Left and right slide, up turns, down falls faster and Space drops.
stop
say: That's the Falling Blocks template.
